STEP 1 — Find out what was built. Read [38;2;177;185;249mplays/008-direction-filter/intent.md [38;2;255;255;255mand [38;2;177;185;249mplays/008-direction-filter/plan.md[38;2;255;255;255m, then read the real changes on the [38;2;177;185;249m008-direction-filter [38;2;255;255;255mbranch[12;3Hof the[1Cproject's repositories ([38;2;177;185;249mgit log[38;2;255;255;255m[1Cand [38;2;177;185;249mgit diff [38;2;255;255;255magainst the default branch it was cut from). Where the plan and[4C code disag[2Ce,[1Ct[1Ce CODE is the truth — the plan is[1Conly  [13;3Hwha[1C was intended.[158X[39m[14;3H[18X[38;2;255;255;255m
STEP 2 — Find where it belongs. List [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/ [38;2;255;255;255mand read what is already there.[16;3H- If[1Ca[1Cdocument th[1Cre ALREADY covers[1Cthis play, UPDATE it. Do not [2Cd a second document about the same thing.[17;5HOtherwise place a new document, [1Cespecting the granularity tha[3Clre[1Cdy exists. If there are module folders, they are this product's modules: put the document in the one this [18;3Hplay belongs to, and only [1Create a new module folder if this[1Cpl[1Cy[1Cgenuinely [2C a new[1Cpart of the product. If the docum[1Cn[1Cs are flat, keep th[1Cm fla[1C.[29X[19;3H- If[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cdocumentation/modules/ [38;2;255;255;255mis EMPTY, you ar[2Cchoosing the [1Ctructur[1C. Judge[1Cthe size[1Cof [1Che product from the[1Cvision, the tech stack and the reposi[1Cories, then pick a granularity[20;3Hyou would still be happy with after twenty more plays:[1Ca small product is serv[1Cd well by a few fla[2Cdocuments, a larger on[1C by a handful of[1Cmodule folders. Say [1Cn one li[1Ce why  [21;7Hchose[1Cwhat you[1Cchose.[151X[22;3H- DEPTH LIMIT:[1Conly [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/<name>.md [38;2;255;255;255mor [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/<module>/<name>.md [38;2;255;255;255mare possible. There is no third level — do not try to nest deeper.[39m[23;3H[162X[38;2;255;255;255m
STEP 3 — Write it. Describe the PRODUCT, not the changeset: what this part does, how it behaves, the decisions and constraints worth knowing, and anything a future implementer [25;3Hwould trip ov[1Cr. No changelog, no diff, no "we changed X [1Co[1CY", no rest[1Cting the[1Cinten[1C. Keep it[1Cconcise and concrete. Do no[1C commit[1C— Bu[1Clding commi[1Cs your[1Cdoc[1Cm[1Cnt on the    [26;3Hplay's branch once you finish.[1CThen end[1Cy[1Cur turn with[1Ca[1Cshort statement of what[1Cyou wrote and where — not a[1Cquestion[39m[1C[55X[27;3H[118X[38;2;255;255;255m
