  ⎿  [mAdded[1m[1C30[22m[1Clines[38;2;248;248;242m[2m[5;6H 54 [22m [m
     [38;2;248;248;242m[2m 55 [22m If no bus is heading to the stop, the section is not shown, even if other buses are on the map.                                                                           [m     [38;2;248;248;242m[2m 56 [22m                                                                                                                                                                           [m     [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 57 +[38;2;248;248;242m### Direction filter                                                                                                                                               [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 58 +                                                                                                                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 59 +[38;2;248;248;242mAt a stop served both ways (for example Portagem), a **direction button** sits on its own row                                                                      [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 60 +[38;2;248;248;242munder the section header, above the list (`sheet/DirectionButton.tsx`). Each press cycles the list                                                                 [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 61 +[38;2;248;248;242m**both → outbound → inbound → both**. The logic is pure and lives in `src/domain/directions.ts`.                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 62 +                                                                                                                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 63 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Served directions.** `directionsAtStop` scans every loaded trip, across all day types in                                                                       [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 64 +  [38;2;248;248;242m`tripsByDayType` and not only today's. A stop is served in a direction when at least one trip of                                                                 [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 65 +  [38;2;248;248;242mthat direction calls there **at any stop but its first**. A bus is only in service once it has                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 66 +  [38;2;248;248;242mleft its first stop, so it never approaches that stop. A terminus therefore counts as served in                                                                  [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 67 +  [38;2;248;248;242mone direction only. The button shows only when the stop is served in exactly both directions, and                                                                [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 68 +  [38;2;248;248;242monly in the expanded "Heading to this stop" section. Otherwise the filter is `both`.                                                                             [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 69 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Label.** `Both directions`, or `To ` followed by that direction's distinct trip destinations,                                                                  [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 70 +  [38;2;248;248;242mmost frequent first, with ties in alphabetical order (for example                                                                                                [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 71 +  [38;2;248;248;242m`To Vale das Flores, Serpins, Corvo`). If a direction has no destinations, the label falls back                                                                  [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 72 +  [38;2;248;248;242mto `Outbound` or `Inbound`. A long label is cut with an ellipsis, and the full label is the                                                                      [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 73 +  [38;2;248;248;242mbutton's `title`. The accessible name is `Direction: <label>`, where "Direction: " is visually                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 74 +  [38;2;248;248;242mhidden text.                                                                                                                                                     [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 75 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Filtering.** Only the list is filtered. It stays soonest first, and the 4-row cap applies                                                                      [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 76 +  [38;2;248;248;242mafter filtering. The section still shows as long as a bus is approaching in *either* direction.                                                                  [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 77 +  [38;2;248;248;242mIf the filter leaves no bus, the list is replaced by "No buses in this direction right now."                                                                     [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 78 +  [38;2;248;248;242m(`NO_BUSES_IN_DIRECTION`). The header, its Scheduled badge and the button stay, so the user can                                                                  [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 79 +  [38;2;248;248;242malways cycle back.                                                                                                                                               [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 80 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **State.** In `App.tsx` the choice is stored with the stop id it was made at. When the nearest                                                                   [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 81 +  [38;2;248;248;242mstop changes, it falls back to `both`, and no effect is needed for that. The choice is not                                                                       [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 82 +  [38;2;248;248;242mpersisted, just like `sheetCollapsed`. `directions` is memoised on the stop **id**, because[70X[38;2;80;200;80m[34;6H 83 +  [38;2;248;248;242m`nearest` is a new object on every position update.[110X[38;2;80;200;80m[35;6H 84 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Not affected:** the map markers, their countdown tags and dimming, smart zoom and the locate[67X[m[36;3H   [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 85 +  [38;2;248;248;242mreframe all keep using the unfiltered approaching list.[106X[38;2;80;200;80m[37;6H 86 +[163X[m
